      "reasoning": "I mulliganed to 6 cards and now need to put one card on the bottom. Let me evaluate my new 6-card hand:\n\
\n\
**My hand after mulligan (7 cards, need to put one on bottom):**\n\
1. Balan, Wandering Knight {2}{W}{W} - 3/3 with first strike, double strike with 2+ equipment\n\
2. Fertilid {2}{G} - 0/0 with 2 counters, can fetch lands\n\
3. Forest - Basic land (green)\n\
4. Forest - Basic land (green)  \n\
5. Hunter's Edge {3}{G} - Put +1/+1 counter on creature, then it fights\n\
6. Order of the Golden Cricket {1}{W} - 2/2 that can gain flying for {W}\n\
7. Plains - Basic land (white)\n\
\n\
**Analysis:**\n\
- Much better color distribution: 2 Forests, 1 Plains\n\
- Can play Order of the Golden Cricket on turn 2 (Plains + Forest)\n\
- Fertilid on turn 3 (Forest, Forest, Plains)\n\
- Balan on turn 4 (needs WWW total, have 2 Forests + Plains)\n\
- Hunter's Edge is a combat trick/removal\n\
- The weakest card here is probably Fertilid - it's a 0/0 for 3 mana that needs another mana to activate its ability\n\
- But Fertilid can help fix mana if I need more lands\n\
- Balan is a strong finisher but requires WWW\n\
- Order of the Golden Cricket is a solid 2/2 for 2 mana\n\
\n\
I think I should put Hunter's Edge on the bottom. It's the most expensive card at 4 mana (3G) and is situational removal that requires having a creature. I'd rather keep the creatures and lands.\n\
\n\
Actually wait, looking more carefully: Fertilid is 3 mana (2G) for a 2/2 that can fetch lands, but I already have 3 lands. Hunter's Edge is 4 mana for removal + pump. Order is 2 mana 2/2. Balan is 4 mana 3/3 with upside.\n\
\n\
Given my mana base (2 Forest, 1 Plains), I can't cast Balan reliably until I get another white source. Fertilid could help fetch a Plains. I think I should keep Fertilid for the potential mana fixing.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me think: I have 3 lands, need 4th land to cast either Fertilid or Balan. Hunter's Edge is expensive removal. Order is my only turn 2 play. I think putting Hunter's Edge on the bottom makes sense - it's the most expensive and least essential card.\n\
\n\
