      "reasoning": "Now I need to decide whether to keep this 6-card hand. Let me reevaluate:\n\
\n\
**My 6-card hand after bottoming Hunter's Edge:**\n\
1. Balan, Wandering Knight {2}{W}{W} - 3/3 with first strike, double strike with 2+ equipment\n\
2. Fertilid {2}{G} - 0/0 with 2 counters, can fetch lands  \n\
3. Forest - Basic land (green)\n\
4. Forest - Basic land (green)\n\
5. Order of the Golden Cricket {1}{W} - 2/2 that can gain flying for {W}\n\
6. Plains - Basic land (white)\n\
\n\
**Analysis:**\n\
- 3 lands (2 Forest, 1 Plains) - decent but not great\n\
- Can play Order on turn 2\n\
- Can play Fertilid on turn 3\n\
- Balan requires WWW - with only 1 Plains, I can't cast him until I draw another white source or use Fertilid to fetch one\n\
- No turn 1 play\n\
- Fertilid can help fix mana if I need more lands\n\
- Reasonable curve: turn 2 Order, turn 3 Fertilid, turn 4 potentially Balan if I draw another white source\n\
\n\
This is a keepable 6-card hand. It has early play, some mana fixing potential, and a finisher. The main issue is color requirements for Balan, but Fertilid can help. I'll keep.\n\
\n\
