      "seq": 84,
      "game_seq": 129,
      "reasoning": "My turn 4. I drew another Plains. So hand: Balan, Fertilid, 2 Plains. Battlefield: Danitha (no longer sick), Order, 2 Forests, 1 Plains all untapped. I have 3 untapped lands (2 Forest, 1 Plains) plus I can play a land.\n\
\n\
I can cast Fertilid {2}{G} or play a land. Fertilid costs 3 mana (2 generic + green). I have 3 untapped lands: 2 Forest, 1 Plains. That's enough.\n\
\n\
But I also need to consider my curve. I have Balan {2}{W}{W} in hand - that's 4 mana with double white. I currently have 1 Plains on battlefield, 2 Plains in hand. If I play a Plains this turn, I'll have 2 white sources on battlefield. Next turn I could play another Plains (land drop) and have 3 white sources for Balan.\n\
\n\
Fertilid is a 0/0 that enters with two +1/+1 counters (makes it 2/2). Can remove a counter to fetch a basic land. That could help me get more white sources for Balan.\n\
\n\
Actually, Fertilid can fetch lands when it ETBs? No, it's an activated ability: Remove a +1/+1 counter: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle. That costs 0 mana, just a counter.\n\
\n\
So Fertilid can help me ramp/fix. I think casting Fertilid is good. It gives me a 2/2 body and potential land fetch.\n\
\n\
But I also have Danitha and Order already. Adding another 2/2 is fine.\n\
\n\
Let me play Plains first to have 4 total lands (2 Forest, 2 Plains). Then cast Fertilid using 2 Forest + Plains maybe.\n\
\n\
Actually, Fertilid needs {2}{G}. I can pay with: Forest (G), Forest (G), Plains (generic) = GGG? Wait, that's 3 green. Actually {2}{G} means 2 generic + green. So I need 1 green and 2 generic. I can pay with Forest (green), Forest (generic), Plains (generic). That works.\n\
\n\
Let me play Plains from hand first.\n\
\n\
