      "reasoning": "Combat phase. I have Order (2/2) and Danitha (2/2 with first strike, vigilance, lifelink) that can attack. Balan has summoning sickness.\n\
\n\
Opponent has War-Name Aspirant (2/1) that can block. If I attack with Danitha:\n\
- Danitha has first strike and lifelink\n\
- If opponent blocks with War-Name (2/1), Danitha deals first strike damage first, killing the 2/1 before it deals damage. I gain 2 life.\n\
- If opponent doesn't block, I deal 2 damage and gain 2 life.\n\
\n\
If I attack with Order:\n\
- Order is 2/2\n\
- If opponent blocks with War-Name (2/1), they trade (Order kills War-Name, War-Name deals 1 damage to Order). Order survives with 1 damage.\n\
- If opponent doesn't block, I deal 2 damage.\n\
\n\
I should attack with both. Danitha can safely attack because even if blocked, she kills the blocker and survives with lifelink. Order can attack too, forcing opponent to either take 2 damage or trade their War-Name.\n\
\n\
Actually, if I attack with both and opponent blocks Danitha with War-Name, Danitha kills it first strike, then Order gets through. If opponent blocks Order, Danitha gets through.\n\
\n\
So attacking with both is good. Let me attack with both.\n\
\n\
