      "reasoning": "Honor Guard resolved, sick.\n\
\n\
Now I have two creatures: Danitha 5/5 first strike lifelink vigilance, Honor Guard 3/2.\n\
\n\
I can attack with Danitha (vigilance) and keep Honor Guard back.\n\
\n\
Opponent has Daring Piracy, Goblin Oriflamme, 5 Mountains tapped, Thriving Bluff tapped. They have 1 card in hand.\n\
\n\
If I attack, they may have a blocker? They have no creatures currently. They'll create a Pirate token at beginning of combat (Daring Piracy trigger). That token has menace and haste, can block? Token created at beginning of combat, can block if it's their turn? Actually it's my turn, token is created under their control? Daring Piracy says \"At the beginning of combat on your turn, create a 1/1 red Pirate creature token with menace and haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step.\" Wait, \"on your turn\" means the controller of Daring Piracy's turn. That's opponent's turn. So on opponent's turn they get a token. On my turn, no token.\n\
\n\
Thus they have no blockers. I can attack freely.\n\
\n\
But they might have removal in hand (Firecannon Blast? Already used). They might have something else.\n\
\n\
I'll attack with Danitha.\n\
\n\
Go to combat.\n\
\n\
Pass.\n\
\n\
